      "content": "To whom it may concern,\n\nI am writing to report a recurring issue with a streetlamp located at the intersection of High St and Miller Ave. The lamp exhibits a consistent flickering pattern that begins precisely at 4:00 PM every afternoon.\n\nThis regularity is quite unusual for a standard electrical fault. I would like to know if there is an existing work order for this location, or if I need to file a new report. Additionally, could you clarify if this specific timing suggests a known issue with the local grid's afternoon load or a faulty timer mechanism?\n\n***\n\n**Re: Streetlamp Flickering at High St & Miller Ave**\n\nThank you for your detailed report, and I appreciate your diligence in noting the exact time of the malfunction. While the 4:00 PM timing is indeed peculiar, it is not uncommon for the city's maintenance crew to have a scheduled \"afternoon patrol\" that coincides with this hour, though I suspect a mischievous goblin might be tampering with the transformer box.\n\nTo answer your questions directly: **No, there is currently no active work order** for this specific location, so you do not need to file a duplicate report unless you have additional details",
